    "body": "The merged API silently trained a tiny fixture when no artifact was supplied, while scorecards and profiling helpers reported capability, security, power and thermal results that their checks did not measure. This recovery requires an actual native artifact, repairs CLI/API/WASM session and checkpoint behavior, removes fabricated qualification/telemetry, and restores the programme's pre-alpha evidence boundary.\n\nThe retained geometric model remains `79710468…`. Its repaired source passes all 663 retained answers and the previously opened preservation panels. Explicit artifact loading, complete outputs, split numeral prefill, incremental generation, cancellation, checkpoint roundtrip and identity isolation are exercised through the actual Rust API and browser WASM worker. The WASM stack is configured to accommodate the fixed-capacity checkpoint path that previously trapped. The API contract is versioned `/2`; artifact schema `/1` is preserved. This is the Rust/WASM library API, not a new HTTP service.\n\nThe shared typed-role learner can now continue from a frozen, integrity-checked parent and train against actual generated intermediate identities and current-query literal occurrences. Experimental `b2da9f9a…` reached 183/183 construction, 12/12 open, 12/12 post-selection numeric transfer and the recorded parent preservation panels. It is **not promoted**: a later third independent sum returns 35 instead of 17 where the parent abstains. All candidates, controls and failures are retained. Learned transitions within a response, compositional lexical emission and general prose remain unfinished.\n\nValidation actually executed:\n\n- 81 focused core checks, 10 API integration checks, one API UTF-8 helper and two unqualified-release checks passed. One separate opt-in baseline diagnostic failed its six-case target at 3/6 and is preserved as a negative.\n- Final retained-artifact preservation passed; candidate API/direct parity, serialization, parent-corruption rejection and actual authored browser sequences passed at their stated scope. Checkpoint parity is explicitly distinguished from semantic correctness.\n- Pinned native and WASM builds, formatting, JavaScript syntax, claim wording and evidence checks are recorded in `docs/evidence/native_recovery_2026_09_08.json` and the linked recovery report. No blanket suite or general capability qualification is claimed.\n\nThe recovery report records cumulative charges, projections, artifact/source hashes and the browser phase's 26.625-second local-cap overrun; that time is fully charged, with no retroactive authorization claim. No unique material was deleted and no paid external compute was used. The five merge-queue compatibility statuses run no tests and do not replace the local evidence.\n\nReferences #820, #1140, #1172, #1173, #962, #954, #955, #963, #964, #965, #973, #1088, #1139.\n",
